[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:68. Persistent]
[00:00.660]Passage 68 | 文章六十八
[00:02.585]Persistent | 坚忍不拔的
[00:04.950]I crossed the street to avoid meeting him, | 我穿过马路，以免遇见他，
[00:09.085]but he saw me and came running towards me. | 但他看见了我，便朝我跑来。
[00:12.840]It was no use pretending that I had not seen him, | 假装没看见他已无用，
[00:16.310]so I waved to him. | 于是我向他挥手。
[00:18.370]I never enjoy meeting Bert Dykes. | 我从不喜欢遇见伯特·戴克斯。
[00:21.975]He never has anything to do. | 他总是无所事事。
[00:24.990]No matter how busy you are, | 无论你有多忙，
[00:27.470]he always insists on coming with you. | 他总是坚持要和你一起去。
[00:30.475]I had to think of a way of preventing him | 我得想个办法，阻止他
[00:33.920]from following me around all morning. | 整个上午都跟着我。
[00:36.860]'Hello, Bert,' I said. | “你好，伯特，”我说，
[00:39.790]'Fancy meeting you here!' | “真巧在这儿遇见你！”
[00:42.310]'Hello, Elizabeth,' Bert answered. | “你好，伊丽莎白，”伯特回答。
[00:46.070]'I was just wondering how to spend the morning | “我正想着怎么打发上午的时间呢，
[00:49.500]until I saw you. | 直到我看到你。
[00:51.670]You're not busy doing anything, are you?' | 你没在忙什么事吧？”
[00:54.865]'No, not at all,' I answered. | “不，一点也不忙，”我回答。
[00:58.020]'I'm going to—would you mind my coming with you?' | “我正要去——你不介意我跟着你吧？”
[01:01.755]he asked before I had finished speaking. | 他在我话还没说完的时候就问道。
[01:04.905]'Not at all,' I lied. | “一点也不介意，”我撒谎道。
[01:07.475]'But I'm going to the dentist.' | “但我正要去牙医那里。”
[01:10.455]'Then I'll come with you,' he answered. | “那我跟你一起去，”他回答。
[01:13.710]'There's always plenty to read in the waiting-room.' | “候诊室总有很多东西可以看。”